Having it there would make possible to check how ther language is supposed
to be parsed. I agree it's not easy and would require a deep understanding
on how the grammar has been implemented, however it would serve as a basis
for any possible discussion on formal grammars.

If you simply put it in a file somewhere on the 'Net, how can you guarantee
that a future reader of CLL will have access to the right version?

If I remember correctly the YACC grammar had to be tweakened somehow to
resolve some ambiguity that the EBNF still had.

Removing the chapter on formal grammar would only save 30-40 pages, I
guess. I would prefer to continue having them in.



